  "summary": "Ibn al-Haytham, known in the West as Alhazen, is placed by MacTutor at about 965 to about 1040, possibly born in Basra and dying in Cairo. Working in Egypt under the Fatimid caliph al-Hakim, he wrote the seven-volume Book of Optics, which explained vision as light coming from objects into the eye.",
